From: Dave Huang <khym@bga.com>
To: catfish@alltel.net
Date: Sat, 23 Dec 2000 22:21:08 +0000
Subject: Re: ldconfig?

On Sat, 23 Dec 2000, T. Martin wrote:
>  Hello,
> I've been curious how come 1.4 and 1.5 doesn't have ldconfig the man pages
> are there.
>  Any plans to fix this, or am I missing something?

NetBSD/alpha uses ELF, and doesn't use ldconfig... check out the NetBSD
ELF FAQ at http://www.netbsd.org/Documentation/elf.html

The manpage is there because NetBSD installs manpages for all ports (so
the manpages can be shared on a file server, for example), and some
ports still use a.out and ldconfig.
